### Food Rescue Berlin - example REST calls
### Open this file in IntelliJ and click the green arrow next to a request.
### These are the same calls the web page's JavaScript makes automatically -
### useful here mainly to demonstrate the error handling quickly.

### 1. All fridges
GET http://localhost:8081/api/fridges

### 2. Only fridges that are in service
GET http://localhost:8081/api/fridges?activeOnly=true

### 3. One fridge with its filling level
GET http://localhost:8081/api/fridges/1/summary

### 4. Everything inside fridge 1
GET http://localhost:8081/api/fridges/1/items

### 5. Register a new fridge
POST http://localhost:8081/api/fridges
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fridge at the sports club",
  "address": "Sportplatzweg 3",
  "district": "Spandau",
  "capacity": 10,
  "active": true
}

### 6. Donate food into fridge 1
POST http://localhost:8081/api/fridges/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pumpkin soup, 3 portions",
  "category": "COOKED_MEAL",
  "quantityKg": 2.4,
  "expiryDate": "2030-01-01",
  "donorName": "Volkskueche"
}

### 7. Claim an item (change the id to one that is still available)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/items/1/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimedBy": "Lena"
}

### 8. Food that must be taken within two days
GET http://localhost:8081/api/items/expiring?days=2

### 9. Impact statistics of the whole network
GET http://localhost:8081/api/stats

### 10. Error example: fridge does not exist -> 404 with a clean JSON message
GET http://localhost:8081/api/fridges/999

### 11. Error example: best-before date in the past -> 409
POST http://localhost:8081/api/fridges/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Yesterday's salad",
  "category": "COOKED_MEAL",
  "quantityKg": 1.0,
  "expiryDate": "2020-01-01"
}

### 12. Error example: missing fields -> 400 with a list of field errors
POST http://localhost:8081/api/fridges
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "address": "",
  "district": "",
  "capacity": 0
}
